  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000123267,
      "SummaryText": "Degesch America Inc. (DAI) is highly committed to the safe handling of Aluminum Phosphide (AlP) and Phosphine (PH3) through having robust prevention and emergency response policies in place. DAI follows strict protocols that are aligned with the Environmental Protection Agency\u0092s (EPA) Risk Management Program (RMP) and OSHA\u0092s Process Safety Management (PSM) standards. Senior leadership actively supports and engages in fostering a culture of safety. Leadership ensures that all employees are trained, emergency preparedness is prioritized, and that procedures are reviewed on a regular basis.\n\nThe facility is located in Fresno, CA. This facility focuses on the distribution of aluminum phosphide (AlP), magnesium phosphide (Mg3P2) and phosphine (PH3). These products are used in the production and storage of agricultural products to control insect pests. These products are used in controlled environments and only by licensed applicators. The quantity of PH3 we intend to store is approximately up to 13,000 pounds, which is above the 5,000 pound threshold limit set by the EPA for applicability to the RMP. \n\nDAIs prevention program includes: \n\u0095\tCompliance with OSHA PSM and EPA RMP regulations\n\u0095\tPerimeter security and intrusion detection\n\u0095\tGas monitoring system for early detection of PH3 leaks\n\u0095\tEmployee training in PH3 specific hazards and the use of PPE\n\u0095\tRoutine equipment inspection and maintenance protocols\n\u0095\tAdequate ventilation\n\nAt DAI, no incidents have occurred in the past five years. This is a reflection of the company\u0092s dedication to safe practices, effective controls, and adherence to operational procedures. \n\nOur emergency response protocols include: \n\u0095\tCoordination with the local fire department and emergency response personnel\n\u0095\tOn-site emergency respiratory equipment (SCBAs) in addition to PPE\n\u0095\tAlarm notification systems\n\nPlanned Changes to Improve Safety: \n\u0095\tA 24/7 fixed gas monitoring system is being installed in warehouse to replace the current portable units"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000123267,
      "SummaryText": ". Portable units will continue to be used for supplemental and perimeter monitoring, as needed.\n\u0095\tContinuous review and improvement of employee training program for emergency response"
    }
  ]
